# What travels with a release, as opposed to what lives in the repository.
#
# `vcpkg_from_github` downloads GitHub's source tarball, which `git archive`
# builds and which honours these. Vendoring the library meant vendoring its
# research record with it: `tools/` alone is 61% of the tracked lines, almost
# all of it the parity ledger's JSON, and `src/README.md` already says it is
# never installed.
#
# `docs/` stays. The generated API reference is what a consumer reads, and the
# README links to it.
#
# A clone still has everything; this only shapes the archive.
tools/         export-ignore
.github/       export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
